  "body": "Process change: yes\n\nWhat changed\n- `cargo xtask gate quick`, `batch` and `release` plan one step for each test target of the debug suites, as the heavy lanes do (#1714). Step names: `<crate> suites: lib`, `bins`, `<binary>`, `doc`.\n- Batch and release start with one build step (`cargo test --no-run`). Quick builds one time for each crate when the crate has more than one run step.\n- Each step has its own log, time and pass or fail line. `--only \"app suites: cmds\"`, `--failed` and `--dry-run` work for one step.\n- Batch keeps `lib` and the binaries, without `SLOW_BINARIES` (as before). Release adds `bins` and `doc`. The ui steps keep CWD `crates/ui`.\n- The gate skill, the AGENTS.md tier table and the xtask usage text describe the new steps.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1941-gate-step-per-binary.md` (steps run in the same order as before; release keeps its waves; a step runs `cargo test -p x --test b`, no direct exe).\n\nPlan sizes (`--dry-run`, this tree)\n| Tier | Steps before | Steps after |\n|---|---|---|\n| batch | 10 | 713 |\n| release | 189 | 911 |\n| quick (for a diff) | one step for each crate | one step for each target, and a build step |\n\nMeasured (Windows, this machine)\n- 7 geometry targets, build ready: one grouped cargo call 1.5 s. Seven steps through `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"geometry suites\"`: 5.0 s. So one cargo start is about 0.5 s. No step rebuilt anything (each ran in 0 s).\n- Estimate, not measured: about 6 min more serial time in batch for 713 steps.\n- Not measured: a full batch gate before and after (about 20 min each), and any Linux runner time. The release wave parallelism is unchanged.\n- Follow-up #1951 (P7): run the exes from the cargo JSON paths to remove the cargo start.\n\nPinning tests (`cargo test -p xtask`, 141 pass)\n- `step_tests::release_runs_every_target_of_every_crate_one_step_each`\n- `step_tests::batch_runs_lib_and_each_non_slow_binary_one_step_each`\n- `step_tests::only_and_failed_select_one_binary_step`\n- Updated: `tests::batch_skips_slow_binaries_and_release_runs_everything` and the quick plan tests.\n\nTest count: no `#[test]` changed in the crates. The step targets of each crate equal the targets of `cargo test -p <crate>` (batch: minus `bins`, `doc` and the slow binaries, as before). The step tests pin this for every crate.\n\nReal runs: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (xtask unit tests, green) and `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"geometry suites\"` (7 steps, green). Not run: a full batch or release gate; a quick gate over app or ui steps.\n\nChangelog: Gate: quick, batch and release plan one step for each test binary, with its own log and time.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1941\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
